        "subject": "LU-21167 tests: wait for NOCREATE to clear after sanity 413Aa",
        "message": "LU-21167 tests: wait for NOCREATE to clear after sanity 413Aa\n\nsanity test_413Aa marks every MDT NOCREATE and then clears\nmdt.*.no_create at exit, but the client keeps the NOCREATE state\nof each MDT until its statfs is refreshed. That happens only on\n\"lfs df\" or similar, since QoS and round-robin mkdir skip NOCREATE\nMDTs without refreshing them. The following tests that rely on\nQoS or round-robin mkdir (413a to 413d and 413h) then see no\nusable MDT and create every directory on the parent MDT, failing\nwith \"N subdirs on MDT0\" or \"subdirs are not evenly distributed\".\n\nWait at the end of 413Aa until \"lfs df\" no longer reports any\nNOCREATE MDT.\n\nFixes: ca3b6bc1436a (\"LU-16507 lmv: fix divide by zero in QoS mkdir\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ide41bd994420aaef809612da7f280b8d96950876\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70926\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
